{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery","id":1191993,"title":"Creation of Free Council - Equality as Mystery?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-05T10:51:04-08:00","id":1191993,"title":"Creation of Free Council - Equality as Mystery?","content":"I'm in very early planing of historical <b>Mage</b> 2E chronicle about Nameless War and creation of Free Council. When I started thinking about this plot more, I remembered how important are to Mage 2E the Mysteries as story fuel. Basically - it's not <b>MtAw</b> 2E if p\u0142ot is not revolving about some Mystery. As I wanted to make chronicle about clearly political topic - creation of new ( Global) Order /Sect - I have a large conundrum. <b>How to make political matter into (supernatural) Mystery for PCs to uncover?</b><br /> <br /> And then it hit me - If Exarchs are Living symbols of Tyranny that Seers uncovered and studies - maybe Free Council members can find forces representing Equality / Democracy? That Nameless PCs will create Free Council to use power of those 'things', like Seers use Tyranny? And here is our topic - If that would be the case -<b> What would be those 'Forces of Equality'? Maybe Atlantean Royality that build Watchtowers?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-05-2018, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T12:05:38-08:00","id":1192016,"title":"","content":"The FC politics are an outgrowth of their three core tenets which are already based on a Mystery.<br /> <br /> Humanity is Magical- The Mystery the FC is built on. A phenomenon that appears to allow humanity to influence the Supernal, upending the idea that hierarchies are the natural order of existence with everything flowing down from the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Destroy the Followers of the Lie- The architects of the Lie are the Exarchs, and the Exarchs are an hierarchical structure of reality that refutes the the Mystery of Humanity is Magical that the FC believe in. Obviously their followers are not only working to destroy that sacred Mystery, but are also reflections of the Exarchs themselves because of Platonism, and so must be destroyed in order to increase the chances of studying magical humanity. Incidentally, they\u2019re also warping the Supernal because the FC believe in that kind of bottom -&gt; up influence.<br /> <br /> Democracy Seeks Truth- If the above two points are true, reality doesn\u2019t just flow down from the Supernal because humanity is magical, and those who seek to create hierarchies to destroy that Mystery, then as a reaction the opposite of hierarchies (Democracy) must be maintained to study, manipulate and grow the magical humanity Mystery.<br /> <br /> If you just chuck something into the setting that acts as a counterweight to the Exarchs by being a force for democracy that isn\u2019t the Free Council itself you\u2019ll just be watering down the Free Council st best, or warping then into mirrorhouse Seers at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-05-2018, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T19:33:07-08:00","id":1192116,"title":"","content":"Looking over Tenets of future Free Council maybe real answer on the topic of main chronicle Mystery.<br /> <br /> <b>Humanity is Magical</b> - It's not doing many things to the revolutionary and democratic impulses of Nameless War beside 'we all are Nameless and working &lt;&lt;humans&gt;&gt; magic, overthrowing Awakened high-class'. So I will move past this in rest of deliberations.<br /> <br /> <b>Democracy Seeks Truth </b>- It's nice slogan of future Free Council - But's what does it really means, as Mystery? Because, nowadays, it looks like political advise: 'And mage governing should be democratic, to unfolding the Truth'. And there is nothing... well, 'mysterious' about it. However, if we reverse and change this statement ( like in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boolean_algebra\" target=\"_blank\">Boolean algebra</a> ) we get that '<b>Truth Points to Democracy</b>'. And this means that some elements in <b>MtAw</b> setting <i>should</i> support Democracy as force in universe. Solving what would be those 'Forces Pointing to Democracy' would be really answer on the topic's Mystery behind creation of Free Council - at least, from narrative point.<br /> <br /> Going further, if <b>Truth Points to Democracy</b> - so ( by Boolean algebra ) <b>Hierarchies are Pointing</b> <b>to Lie. </b>It's not far from the <b>Destroy the Followers of the Lie </b>that is next official tenet of once created Council. So fixing on statement <b>Hierarchies are Pointing to Lie </b>should connect the plot of chronicles to creation of two of three Free Council tenets.<br /> <br /> <b>Okay, but HOW to implement 'Hierarchies are Pointing to Lie' in living, action game?</b> <b>And for that matter - How can you point that something is 'Pointing to Lie' in Mage, in the first place? </b>MtAw is not 'Matrix' universe to say 'they are machine, they are fake'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T20:09:56-08:00","id":1192127,"title":"","content":"Humanity is Magical is a (And the -only-) Mystery (Of the FC), and you're failing to engage with it as such. The two other tenets that follow from it are political motivations that cause them to protect that first tenet, which is the Mystery they obsess over.<br /> <br /> You would be better served to focus on creating elements in your setting that point to Humanity is Magical as an overarching theme. Democracy vs. Heirarchy(The Lie) should be the lens you use to paint the picture of how the nascent FC view the conflict. Hierarchies are bad because they crush the idea that Humanity is Magical. Democracy is good because it's the opposite of how Heirarchies work, and so support Humanity is Magical.<br /> <br /> From the FC position it's obvious that Hierarchies point to the Lie. All other Mages believe that reality is a Platonic relationship, the Supernal shape the Fallen, but the FC has observed that the Fallen is able to shape the Supernal, which is the complete and polar opposite. The group that most reverently adheres to this ideology are the Seers, and they are also the most strictly hierarchical faction of Mages. Couple that with the fact that almost every Mage (Including Seers) believes that the Exarchs created the Lie in the first place means that the true potential of Humanity is Magical cannot be realized while servants of the Lie continue to work in the Fallen twisting the Supernal, and Hierarchies must be overthrown via Democracy because the architects of Hierarchies are the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T20:12:37-08:00","id":1192129,"title":"","content":"I dunno, reversing Democracy Seeks Truth to Truth Seeks Democracy is one of those subtle but significant changes to the setting and lore to me. In Awakening we have the Supernal as the objective Truth, but because we are fallible and Fallen, we have many differing perspectives on it... and thus, different ways to reach the Truth. Awakened society was for centuries dead certain that the Awakened City model was the only feasible way to Truth... until a bunch of Nameless Orders figured out that, no, there is another way. And said way happens to be an anachronistic set of governance nobody really cared about for the past few centuries. Which suddenly rose as the dominant political ideology of the world, almost as if the World itself was backing up the Council\u2019s claims. That is a Mystery enough for me... but then again, I major in politics, so I\u2019m biased towards things like this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However! Let\u2019s say we do reverse it like you want, having Truth Points to Democracy and thus Hierarchy Fosters the Lie. Then... wouldn\u2019t the Seers be enough proof of that? I mean, that\u2019s their religion and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T20:20:29-08:00","id":1192132,"title":"","content":"There's only one Mystery the FC as an organization cares about. Humanity is Magical. It doesn't take a whole lot of fucking looking to realize that the Seers and their Exarchs would want to wipe that Mystery out of existence. Their other two tenets are their to protect -their- Mystery. The FC can only just barely stand the Diamond Orders because they're at least not actively welshing on their Mystery with their entire might. At worst the other Orders see it as disruptive to their own Myteries, but they can at least entertain the idea of it. The Seers can't, because it would mean acknowledging that the Exarchs are not the end all, be all of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T22:06:48-08:00","id":1192149,"title":"","content":"<i>Remember in this discussion </i>- <b>I thinking about chronicles of Nameless slowly <i>becoming</i> modern Free Council in whole 19th century all stories will be, probably with many characters. </b>Like with any <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_movement\" target=\"_blank\">Social Movement</a>, 'founding fathers' did not had ready answers the FC is joined together now. They will seek answers to some questions that will drill them - and some answers in all those Nameless groups will <b><i>not be</i></b> what future Free Council in the end will be. Think here about history movements like LGBT+ - in all the last 50 years there were MANY groups of different stances on general problem in movement, some with clearly opposing views. I see creation of Free Council from Nameless the same way. Final tenents of FC maybe consensus made after Great Refusal - but before it, Nameless War as great battle of diffrent ideas what Awakaned society <i>should</i> mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192129#post1192129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakened society was for centuries dead certain that the Awakened City model was the only feasible way to Truth... until a bunch of Nameless Orders figured out that, no, there is another way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nameless Orders had this answer for the Awakened society for centuries, as long as Diamond Orders are. They just were to weak on their own to make a real threat to Diamond and Seers hegemony on whole Atlantis question. And even still they are FC researchers on Awakened City model, don't they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192129#post1192129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And said way happens to be an anachronistic set of governance nobody really cared about for the past few centuries. Which suddenly rose as the dominant political ideology of the world, almost as if the World itself was backing up the Council\u2019s claims. That is a Mystery enough for me... but then again, I major in politics, so I\u2019m biased towards things like this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So you point that Democracy weirdly become in 19th century ideal society, en mass? This is... interesting observation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> How to make it game play Mystery then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192129#post1192129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However! Let\u2019s say we do reverse it like you want, having Truth Points to Democracy and thus Hierarchy Fosters the Lie. Then... wouldn\u2019t the Seers be enough proof of that? I mean, that\u2019s their religion and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's clearly part of the puzzle. But would simply pointing few Nameless 'Seers are evil, they attack you' is the answer to pulling whole Free Council?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T22:32:10-08:00","id":1192151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nameless Orders had this answer for the Awakened society for centuries, as long as Diamond Orders are. They just were to weak on their own to make a real threat to Diamond and Seers hegemony on whole Atlantis question. And even still they are FC researchers on Awakened City model, don't they? </div> </div> </div>I was referring to \u2018answer\u2019 as in a universal structure for Awakened society, rather than structure for \u201cour Nameless order\u2019s society.\u201d Or was there a Nameless order, pre-Council, have indeed an ideology that can be applied universally as well as that of the big three sects?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you point that Democracy weirdly become in 19th century ideal society, en mass? This is... interesting observation. How to make it game play Mystery then? </div> </div> </div>Hmm... since we\u2019re still talking about Mage, maybe phenomena where the beliefs of the masses are supposedly shaping local Mysteries, like Reality Zones from Ascension?<br /> <br /> EDIT: The above also feeds somewhat into what Mrmdubois said, about the Council\u2019s core Mystery being Humanity Is Magical. Yes, this also goes against Mage\u2019s cosmology. Which is why it\u2019s a good Mystery.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still of the opinion that \u201cHey, democracy wasn\u2019t a thing for ages, but suddenly Sleepers are making it work? What does this say about the Supernal?\u201d is a Mystery itself. But like I said, this probably isn\u2019t interesting enough for your table...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's clearly part of the puzzle. But would simply pointing few Nameless 'Seers are evil, they attack you' is the answer to pulling whole Free Council? </div> </div> </div>The Exarchs, their Mystery Commands and Prelacies. Observation of sentient Supernal symbols of hierarchy commanding earthly mages to encouraging social structures and circumstances that smother enlightenment and Awakening. <br /> <br /> This also means that the early Libertines could have studied the Exarchs extensively, more than the Seers. Ironic, yet fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-06-2018, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T00:25:45-08:00","id":1192164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192151#post1192151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m still of the opinion that \u201cHey, democracy wasn\u2019t a thing for ages, but suddenly Sleepers are making it work? What does this say about the Supernal?\u201d is a Mystery itself. But like I said, this probably isn\u2019t interesting enough for your table...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't necessarily mix the FC version of 'Democracy' with the 19th C. version of democracy. I'd say the latter owes far more to ideas of violent nationalism that sound more like Hegemony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T01:18:24-08:00","id":1192173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192164#post1192164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't necessarily mix the FC version of 'Democracy' with the 19th C. version of democracy. I'd say the latter owes far more to ideas of violent nationalism that sound more like Hegemony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that <i>whole Nameless War</i> started because some Nameless were invited by Hegemony in French Revolution to join them, so it sounds fitting with canon of <b>MtAw</b> gameline...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-06-2018, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T01:48:37-08:00","id":1192178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192151#post1192151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to \u2018answer\u2019 as in a universal structure for Awakened society, rather than structure for \u201cour Nameless order\u2019s society.\u201d Or was there a Nameless order, pre-Council, have indeed an ideology that can be applied universally as well as that of the big three sects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically every new found kingdoms mages that previous Diamond found was Nameless - and not all of the had respected version of their Awakened City - they just seems to rather fit general ideas of Darshanas and Diamond <i>convinced</i> them 'we are all hiers to glorious Atlantis!' - Case in point - Mutapa Empire Awakened society from <b>Dark Eras Companion</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192151#post1192151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... since we\u2019re still talking about Mage, maybe phenomena where the beliefs of the masses are supposedly shaping local Mysteries, like Reality Zones from Ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not read a lot of Ascension - maybe corebook, almost two decades now ago. Could you shine this Reality Zones phenomena from <b>MtAs</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192151#post1192151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m still of the opinion that \u201cHey, democracy wasn\u2019t a thing for ages, but suddenly Sleepers are making it work? What does this say about the Supernal?\u201d is a Mystery itself. But like I said, this probably isn\u2019t interesting enough for your table...</div> </div> </div> </div>I must be frank that I like as ST Mysteries that you can be, metaphorically, 'punch in the face'. Observation about democracy return in 19th century is interesting - but how to make it into antagonist or supernatural investigation with plot twists? Could you make some <i>thing</i> that is for or against this rise of Democracy? Thinking now about it - maybe some Exarchs moves that want to stop democratic movement on the world? Some Ochemata? Ministries global actions? Hmmm, maybe some large Seers crossMinistry movement fighting with Democracy - some 19th century Methodology? That connects with your ideas below...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192151#post1192151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exarchs, their Mystery Commands and Prelacies. Observation of sentient Supernal symbols of hierarchy commanding earthly mages to encouraging social structures and circumstances that smother enlightenment and Awakening.<br /> <br /> This also means that the early Libertines could have studied the Exarchs extensively, more than the Seers. Ironic, yet fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T06:52:25-08:00","id":1192232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192164#post1192164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't necessarily mix the FC version of 'Democracy' with the 19th C. version of democracy. I'd say the latter owes far more to ideas of violent nationalism that sound more like Hegemony.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the idea of the nascent Council starting as a subversion of Seer ideology, mirroring how the Seers themselves started as an Exarchal cult within the Diamond, has a certain ironic appeal to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And looking at Mage 2E core's Orders section again, it seems that while the Council shook off nationalism out of democracy, the streak of violence still taints them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T07:13:57-08:00","id":1192245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192178#post1192178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically every new found kingdoms mages that previous Diamond found was Nameless - and not all of the had respected version of their Awakened City - they just seems to rather fit general ideas of Darshanas and Diamond <i>convinced</i> them 'we are all hiers to glorious Atlantis!' - Case in point - Mutapa Empire Awakened society from <b>Dark Eras Companion</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, what I meant was: Did any of those proud Nameless local societies build a social structure that can be convinced to and adapted for any mage around the world they meet? For a few centuries, the Diamond and the Seers were the only ones who could say Yes. Until the Council rose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did not read a lot of Ascension - maybe corebook, almost two decades now ago. Could you shine this Reality Zones phenomena from <b>MtAs</b>? </div> </div> </div>Not too savvy on Ascension lore either, but here's my best: Unlike in Awakening, which has an objective truth in the Supernal that is filtered by different perspectives, Ascension's default stance is that reality is Consensual. The laws of physics as modern science knows only work because a bunch of mages (who'll get pissed if you call them that) worked damn hard to convince the Sleeper masses that they do work. Which means that in the past, you could have things like dragons and giants walking around Europe, square-cube law be damned.<br /> <br /> However, the Consensus isn't universal across the globe. Because truth is subjective, local beliefs shape local reality. Hence, Reality Zones. You can expect things straight out of science fiction work in a closed lab of hyper-advanced science (read; another form of magic), which will fail to work if taken out to the streets. You can expect witchcraft to work in those secluded towns far, far from cities where people's culture and lifestyles haven't changed much from the last century or two, but that witch becomes impotent in the big city.<br /> <br /> Now, how to make this work in Awakening? Well, mages all know already that the Supernal defines the Fallen. Even the to-be-Libertines do. Their theory of human culture conjuring new Supernal symbols is exactly that; a theory. So provide them with areas that serve as proof - where magic conforms to the expectations of the Sleeping masses. Of course, this should be isolated incidents in Awakening, much like how Ansho only happen in Tokyo and the Astral intrusions of Los Angeles, unlike in Ascension where the entire world works that way. What could be causing the Supernal World to become to malleable? Some sort of Prime magic? An obscure form of Emanation? A Bound stirring from its slumber? Or could it be that humanity is indeed magical like the Libertines claim? Or perhaps is this a sign of mass Awakening, something the Silver Ladder would accept? What are the Seers and the Exarchs doing? Better yet, what are they <i>aren't</i> doing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I must be frank that I like as ST Mysteries that you can be, metaphorically, 'punch in the face'. Observation about democracy return in 19th century is interesting - but how to make it into antagonist or supernatural investigation with plot twists? Could you make some <i>thing</i> that is for or against this rise of Democracy? Thinking now about it - maybe some Exarchs moves that want to stop democratic movement on the world? Some Ochemata? Ministries global actions? Hmmm, maybe some large Seers crossMinistry movement fighting with Democracy - some 19th century Methodology? That connects with your ideas below...<br /> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, basically what you say here, along with my translation of Reality Zones as above.<br /> <br /> Though I'd be careful of introducing Ochemata; that's the Exarchs' big guns, which should overwhelm any bunch of non-archmages in-game, and should be used sparingly in out-of-game context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T07:33:09-08:00","id":1192252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192245#post1192245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I'd be careful of introducing Ochemata; that's the Exarchs' big guns, which should overwhelm any bunch of non-archmages in-game, and should be used sparingly in out-of-game context.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>If was going to use Ochemata working for Exarchs - I would put only one of it, working at few points around the world, for whole century. </b>Ochemata would then go to Seers and Sleepers politician to 'convince them' that fresh Democracy is bad idea. Seers would form crossMinistry Methodology around it, Sleepers would be... well. convinced. Most of chronicle stuff then would be stoping particular Seer or Sleeper working for the Ochemata itself. And if PCs would need other mages to overthrow this Supernal Half-God of Tyranny - well, it's time we have creation of future Free Council in it, don't we. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I imagine Ochemata playing roles like Count Taaffe from <i>Affaire Mayerling</i> musical - it's even take place in end of 19th century.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Nc-X1wlU3Q\" data-code=\"2Nc-X1wlU3Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2Nc-X1wlU3Q/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>If going this idea - There is still problem of how to make chronicle so the Nameless PCs would be <i>hurt</i> for the unDemocratic forces from Exarchs?</b> It's not like we already have Free Council that has in it's 'statutory goals' to hunt servants of Tyranny. And I cannot just think of 19th century character that say 'We need Democracy in our lives, as some monsters/forces as trying to stop us'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mages do not have the same needs as lower-classes half-starving Sleepers citizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-06-2018, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T13:40:49-08:00","id":1192377,"title":"","content":"Aaaand that\u2019s where I blank out. Although, as Mrmdubois pointed out, the Council\u2019s ultimate interests lie in preserving humanity\u2019s magical potential found in its culture, so it\u2019s likely the whole thing started from that, and expanded to democracy as a concrete concept only later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:33:44-08:00","id":1192398,"title":"","content":"The whole idea that the Free Council favors democracy is a lie. The last time I checked real democracy's don't condone the whole sale slaughter of everyone who voted against the winners of the last election, which is what happened in &quot;The Great Refusal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:46:51-08:00","id":1192405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192398#post1192398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole idea that the Free Council favors democracy is a lie. The last time I checked real democracy's don't condone the whole sale slaughter of everyone who voted against the winners of the last election, which is what happened in &amp;quot;The Great Refusal.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Mages are too often not the ideals they say they are. Like everyone else. <br /> <br /> The Council\u2019s flavor of Hubris is specifically called out as violence, so the book leaves some wriggle room for Libertines to go to really dark places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T19:42:44-08:00","id":1192498,"title":"","content":"They technically also don't really support Sleepers being involved in their government very much because of the damage Sleepers can do to the other Mysteries their individual members are Obsessed with. If they had their way they'd probably be an open organization, but it wouldn't be a very transparent system regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T00:00:04-08:00","id":1192541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192398#post1192398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole idea that the Free Council favors democracy is a lie. The last time I checked real democracy's don't condone the whole sale slaughter of everyone who voted against the winners of the last election, which is what happened in &quot;The Great Refusal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You've misread it. The Great Refusal predates the forming of the Free Council. It's a co-ordinated plan to gather information through appearing to co-operate with the Seers before launching an all-out attack on the Order. However some of the Nameless actually join the Seers. It's not a vote; it's a plan the Seer Nameless choose to betray. Plenty of real life democracies will execute traitors, especially in times of war.<br /> <br /> Also, most democracies do have provisions for defending their constitutions from elements that want to overthrow it. Signing on with the magic Nazis isn't just a difference of opinion, it's a massive betrayal of everything the order stands for.<br /> <br /> Additionally, they didn't slaughter them all. It's a major plot point in Mage Noir that the FC was willing to burn it's goodwill with the Silver Ladder to reintegrate Seer Nameless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T00:17:50-08:00","id":1192545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192377#post1192377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, as Mrmdubois pointed out, the Council\u2019s ultimate interests lie in preserving humanity\u2019s magical potential found in its culture, so it\u2019s likely the whole thing started from that, and expanded to democracy as a concrete concept only later.</div> </div> </div> </div>It maybe priorities <i>now</i> for Free Council, but Nameless were rag-tag groups of factions and cults, with various goals, sometimes fighting each other in Nameless War. I wanted to run more society conscious story about need for Democracy in Nameless. I just have problem to find the reasons why Nameless would said 'Yes, we need to find and implement Democracy, like Sleepers do'. Because Nameless are, well, mages - even simple Arcana get you powers make you a waaayyy ahead of any Sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-07-2018, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T01:07:49-08:00","id":1192550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192545#post1192545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It maybe priorities <i>now</i> for Free Council, but Nameless were rag-tag groups of factions and cults, with various goals, sometimes fighting each other in Nameless War. I wanted to run more society conscious story about need for Democracy in Nameless. I just have problem to find the reasons why Nameless would said 'Yes, we need to find and implement Democracy, like Sleepers do'. Because Nameless are, well, mages - even simple Arcana get you powers make you a waaayyy ahead of any Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... is there any other form of governance that can balance the teeming mass of disparate perspectives into a united political power, while also protecting the differences between those perspectives?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not necessarily about learning from Sleepers; it\u2019s about finding what matters. Which happened to be something Sleepers found first. I see no reason why mages wouldn\u2019t adopt anything from Sleepers just because they were magically more potent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T01:12:50-08:00","id":1192552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192550#post1192550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... is there any other form of governance that can balance the teeming mass of disparate perspectives into a united political power, while also protecting the differences between those perspectives?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not necessarily about learning from Sleepers; it\u2019s about finding what matters. Which happened to be something Sleepers found first. I see no reason why mages wouldn\u2019t adopt anything from Sleepers just because they were magically more potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>You talk about 'mages using Democracy as political structure of their society'. I talk that I would want to stir chronicle into 'Democracy as supernatural Mystery Nameless try to grasp'. I have a problem with PCs getting 'Aha, Democracy CAN BE magical Mystery we should seek' moment, to clash PCs with Ochemata antagonists goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T01:17:06-08:00","id":1192553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192552#post1192552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You talk about 'mages using Democracy as political structure of their society'. I talk that I would want to stir chronicle into 'Democracy as supernatural Mystery Nameless try to grasp'. I have a problem with PCs getting 'Aha, Democracy CAN BE magical Mystery we should seek' moment, to clash PCs with Ochemata antagonists goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, how about the Consensual Reality Zone I talked about earlier?<br /> <br /> Frankly, that\u2019s all I can think of the moment, because I\u2019m still firmly on the interpretation that Democracy isn\u2019t a <i>central</i> Mystery for the Council; that\u2019d be the various Cultures, which Democracy as a concept helps protecting (well, better than the Ocean City model of the Diamond and the Seers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T03:12:09-08:00","id":1192565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192552#post1192552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You talk about 'mages using Democracy as political structure of their society'. I talk that I would want to stir chronicle into 'Democracy as supernatural Mystery Nameless try to grasp'. I have a problem with PCs getting 'Aha, Democracy CAN BE magical Mystery we should seek' moment, to clash PCs with Ochemata antagonists goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019d have an easier time focusing on Humanity is Magical as your A Mystery, and then have your B plot be the formation of these ideas about democracy that start emerging in the Nameless culture as a result.<br /> <br /> Because, y\u2019know, that\u2019s how it happened in the canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T03:43:07-08:00","id":1192571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192565#post1192565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You\u2019d have an easier time focusing on Humanity is Magical as your A Mystery, and then have your B plot be the formation of these ideas about democracy that start emerging in the Nameless culture as a result.<br /> <br /> Because, y\u2019know, that\u2019s how it happened in the canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>We <b>do not have canon</b> for what exactly happened in 19th century ( as at least I know <b>Mage</b> gameline books ). We are only pointed that Nameless War started when some Nameless were asked by the Seers of Throne in French Revolution. And War ended with Great Refusal. From what I found on canon until now - we do not know what exactly happened between.<br /> <br /> Also, <i>Humanity is Magical</i> do not seems as plot and conflict leading Mystery. It looks: 'Ow, you can mage magic from humans science or voodoo rituals? Cool. I want to be taught that.' And that's basically all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192553#post1192553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, that\u2019s all I can think of the moment, because I\u2019m still firmly on the interpretation that Democracy isn\u2019t a <i>central</i> Mystery for the Council; that\u2019d be the various Cultures, which Democracy as a concept helps protecting (well, better than the Ocean City model of the Diamond and the Seers)</div> </div> </div> </div>I still stand that it maybe not central to Council that is <i>now </i>- but it need to be in some factions at Nameless War so the Democracy become so large part of Council later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-07-2018, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T12:35:49-08:00","id":1192711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/equality/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://plato.stanford.edu/symbols/sep-man-red.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/equality/\" target=\"_blank\"> Equality (Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy) </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/equality/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/equality/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T16:01:01-08:00","id":1192832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192571#post1192571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We <b>do not have canon</b> for what exactly happened in 19th century ( at least I know <b>Mage</b> gameline books ). We are only pointed that Nameless War started when some Nameless were asked by the Seers of Throne in French Revolution. And War ended with Great Refusal. From what I found on canon until now - we do not know what exactly happened between.<br /> <br /> Also, <i>Humanity is Magical</i> do not seems as plot and conflict leading Mystery. It looks: 'Ow, you can mage magic from humans science or voodoo rituals? Cool. I want to be taught that.' And that's basically all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, there's nothing specific, -but- we do know that the central Mystery that pulled the Free Council together is Humanity is Magical, because it's their investigation into that particular Mystery that ended up coalescing them into a powerful faction of Mages across the world with a political agenda geared toward protecting their collective ability to dig into that Mystery.<br /> <br /> Also, you're looking at Humanity is Magical from the wrong angle. We're talking Supernal Entities or Verges that appear to have always existed, but are also closely tied to documented human phenomena that's only cropped up in the last few centuries or decades. We're talking about Seers freaking out and trying to subvert or destroy cults, artifacts or places that seem to point to the idea that Humanity is Magical. We're talking about Ley Lines being moved by human architecture or terra-forming. We're talking about the Astral exploding with new realms as people discover new ideas and start to talk and think about them. We're talking about hedge witches, and psychics doing stuff Mages can only do with significantly more risk. We're talking about completely normal Sleepers starting to do things with technology that Mages couldn't even imagine, just take advantage of once it exists.<br /> <br /> Your idea of Humanity is Magical is far, far too limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:32:20-08:00","id":1192924,"title":"","content":"The fundamental disconnect of what people are suggesting and what you seek for, wyrdhamster, comes from a crucial difference of perspective in how the Free Coucil works, so...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Not that I wouldn\u2019t want to see what comes out of \u201cdemocracy as a Mystery,\u201d though. Precisely because that\u2019s not what the book focuses on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-07-2018, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:58:55-08:00","id":1192935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, there's nothing specific, -but- we do know that the central Mystery that pulled the Free Council together is Humanity is Magical, because it's their investigation into that particular Mystery that ended up coalescing them into a powerful faction of Mages across the world with a political agenda geared toward protecting their collective ability to dig into that Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only your opinion, not supported on any canon - do not remember single line in gameline that <i>Humanity is Magical</i> being the Council Mystery that started unification from Nameless War. At least from what I see in text - it's Great Refusal to Seers that joined future Council.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you're looking at Humanity is Magical from the wrong angle. We're talking Supernal Entities or Verges that appear to have always existed, but are also closely tied to documented human phenomena that's only cropped up in the last few centuries or decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>New 'suits' for Supernal powers on Earth is something that comes for <i>millenia</i>. Arcadia's Anachronisms can be Greek muse-like being - or clockwork robot. It's not in any way special for the 19th century - just 'suits' changed then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about Seers freaking out and trying to subvert or destroy cults, artifacts or places that seem to point to the idea that Humanity is Magical.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing canon in this interpretation - but good pointing on general Seers attitude at that time. Still, it's not pointing that Free Council comes up from 'Seers are going after our Nameless cults'... Wait, it <i>does</i> feel for this. If Diamond left Nameless on their own and Seers are there to kick their asses - Nameless needs to organise. And <i>then</i> taking Democracy for them have sense - as opposition to the 'corrupted elits system' of Diamond.<br /> <br /> Still, it does nothing on pointing how to engage PCs in the Seers conflict idea in the first place...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about Ley Lines being moved by human architecture or terra-forming.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Diamond mages were doing for <i>millenia</i> till that time. Or some Sleepers building their stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about the Astral exploding with new realms as people discover new ideas and start to talk and think about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Diamond mages were doing for <i>millenia</i> till that time. It's not that in only 19th century people were inventing new things - civilization was inventing and forgetting things for centuries now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about hedge witches, and psychics doing stuff Mages can only do with significantly more risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by that? I do not understand what you pointing here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about completely normal Sleepers starting to do things with technology that Mages couldn't even imagine, just take advantage of once it exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>This <i><b>is</b></i> a bit new thing in a setting. I already for years was thinking of using Gifted inventors and mad scientists from <b>Mage Chronicles Guide </b>in this FC chronicle idea. However, beside one players taking Gifted as PC and others doing 'ow, you are sooo exotic and mysterious' - it's not leading chronicle plot. The best it would be sub-plot, about Gifted under attempts from Seers to be recruited on their side. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192832#post1192832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your idea of Humanity is Magical is far, far too limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the end, I just do not found <i>Humanity is Magical</i> very much different from the what Diamond was doing by millenia. Diamond already found promising mages from <b>very</b> different backgrounds and offered them membership in their exclusive club. BUT it does lead idea to Democracy - if PCs Nameless are those that were overturned by Diamond in first place, they have so much better reason to try to start their own society, based on Democracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's still not the story hook based on Democracy as Mystery... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T20:44:43-08:00","id":1192951,"title":"","content":"If you read the three core tenets of the FC it's pretty obvious to me that the only one that's actually concerned with a Mystery is Humanity is Magical and that the other two were constructed to protect their ability to dig into Humanity is Magical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> New 'suits' for Supernal powers on Earth is something that comes for <i>millenia</i>. Arcadia's Anachronisms can be Greek muse-like being - or clockwork robot. It's not in any way special for the 19th century - just 'suits' changed then. </div> </div> </div>Why does the change suit them? Why do Supernal constructs modernize? Because Humanity is Magical and can change the Supernal. Then the Supernal retro-editing kicks in after a change is made and it's always been that way, but there are always weird little after-effects left behind because of humanity inflicted Aponoia. You seriously can't do something cool with that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is nothing canon in this interpretation </div> </div> </div> Yes, there is, it's part of the Seers core mission to keep the Sleepers asleep. If Humanity realized it's Magical that'd be the most major fuck-up they've ever had. You seriously can't make a plot out of that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Diamond mages were doing for <i>millenia</i> till that time. Or some Sleepers building their stuff. </div> </div> </div> Mages can do it with magic, humans can do it by laying some bricks on top of each other or rearranging the landscape. Technically, Mages could do it that way too, but humans do it -way- more often considering how much they outnumber Mages. You never thought about being curious why Sleepers can affect the mystical landscape so much?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Diamond mages were doing for <i>millenia</i> till that time. It's not that in only 19th century people were inventing new things - civilization was inventing and forgetting things for centuries now. </div> </div> </div> No, Mages explore the Astral, they have some small part to play in creating and manipulating it, but Sleepers have managed to blow out a huge portion of the Astral and turn it into the Temenos all by themselves. You don't think that's magic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This <i><b>is</b></i> a bit new thing in a setting. I already for years was thinking of using Gifted inventors and mad scientists from <b>Mage Chronicles Guide </b>in this FC chronicle idea. However, beside one players taking Gifted as PC and others doing 'ow, you are sooo exotic and mysterious' - it's not leading chronicle plot. The best it would be sub-plot, about Gifted under attempts from Seers to be recruited on their side </div> </div> </div> You have completely missed my point. Sleepers can do things Mages can do even if it takes them longer to get there, and particularly when considering Gross Arcanum stuff. Sleepers, completely mundane people are also always coming up with ideas about how the world works that Mages would never have considered on their own, and a surprising amount of the time they're getting it right. Did you ever even pay attention to what the standard tool for a member of the FC is?<br /> <br /> Part of your problem is you look at Humanity is Magical and think it's obvious, but you have to look at it from all sides. The Seers see it and are scared shitless and get very, very nasty about it. The Diamond see it, but they look at it as a bug that's gotta be pinned to a board, examined and explained away, they are the all powerful Mages who know best and are better than people (Stellar examples being the Ladder and the Mysterium). The Free Council see it and yeah, they want to study it, but they also want to see it grow, they want to see what it can do when properly supported.<br /> <br /> Democracy isn't a Mystery, it's a well defined and understood political structure despite it's many variations. Even if it was a Mystery do you know who made it? HUMANS! Because Humanity is Magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-08-2018, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T02:42:10-08:00","id":1193027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192571#post1192571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I just do not found <i>Humanity is Magical</i> very much different from the what Diamond was doing by millenia. Diamond already found promising mages from <b>very</b> different backgrounds and offered them membership in their exclusive club.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fundamentally different.<br /> <br /> The Diamond sees magic as filtering down from the Supernal. If sleeper sciences and traditions have elements of real supernal knowledge, that's because the sleepers picked it up from the Supernal.<br /> <br /> The FC believe that humans produce symbols and those then alter the Supernal. It's a bottom up approach. The Sleepers don't just passively receive Supernal symbolism, they produce it as well.<br /> <br /> Now, in theory that's maybe not that radical, however the Diamond is fundamentally based on the belief that the Supernal is supreme over humanity. They divide into four castes because that's what they believe the Supernal says they should be. Masters justify their hold on power within the Diamond because they're the ones closest to the Supernal. Even the ideologies of each Diamond Order are fundamentally based on that belief.<br /> <br /> The FC challenge that. If even sleepers can make their own truths, then what right does a Master have dictate the truth? It radically challenges everything the Diamond stand for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T02:53:24-08:00","id":1193859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1193027#post1193027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The FC challenge that. If even sleepers can make their own truths, then what right does a Master have dictate the truth? It radically challenges everything the Diamond stand for.</div> </div> </div> </div>And means literally zero on 'Oh yes, we find this next Supernal magic user' from Nameless perspective. It only points that that protoFree Council and Nameless should <i>not</i> joined Diamond. This in-setting Mystery of <i>Humanity is Magical</i> is, in reality, unprovable - as the forces of it can easily be answered on both Diamond <b>and</b> proto-Free Council sides.<br /> <br /> Take a look on Haitan Hoodoon that Awakened in 19th century. Diamond would say 'He has seen the Truth of Stygia!'. Proto-Free Council would say 'He found magic in Voodoo'. Both are right - and both has enough evidence in Supernal mechanics in setting at 19th century it becomes <i>political</i> <i>squabble </i>over Sects.<br /> <br /> Ironicly, but poiniting me the 'need' for exploring <i>Humanity is Magical</i> - you just give me one more point for putting <i>Democracy Points to Truth</i> as more important in creation of Free Council. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If the 'Truth' of Diamond is basically meaningless - the proper Truth should be asserted by Awakened ( and Sleepers ) in ways of Democracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And with sudden rise of Democracy in 19th century in Sleepers we have real strange spread of this 'equality phenomena'. Like something in Supernal Realms were spreading those ideas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-10-2018, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T03:01:00-08:00","id":1193862,"title":"","content":"Now to think what could this Democracy spreading thing be... If Diamond would be right, it simply by some massive move on mass readying-to-Awakening, done by one of Oracles. BUT Oracles are symbols of monarchies in-power ( they are described as Royalty of Atlantis in Diamond myths ). <b>So what could spread magic around humanity, that is not Oracles or Exarchs ( as those are monarchists Supernal deities and Democracy seeking proto-Free Council would try to overthrow views like those ( seeking Democracy in first place to get against rule of Mentors )?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T04:55:39-08:00","id":1193884,"title":"","content":"Did you even read my last post?<br /> <br /> If democracy is a Mystery it\u2019s because it was made by humans because Humanity is Magical. Of course democracy isn\u2019t a mystery, it\u2019s a well understood way to structure human society.<br /> <br /> The claim that you can\u2019t prove that humans can do magic is such utter bullshit. There is an over-abundance of proof. You\u2019re just somehow completely ignorant about it. Humans do magic stuff all the time, the only difference is that they don\u2019t know they\u2019re doing it, and that it typically takes more of them to do it. Your problem is that you just look at it as natural processes. Humanity manipulates reality on a quantum level, the mystic landscape of ley lines, nodes, Hallows, etc, the Astral, the Shadow, devise new forms of life, and on and on! <br /> <br /> Also, don\u2019t forget Mages were human. Literally the most magical people on the planet are created by humans and you say that you can\u2019t prove Humanity is Magical.<br /> <br /> Your insistence on creating a force in the Supernal or whatever to forge the FC really is just making them Seers. I think you\u2019ve just lost the ability to claim you\u2019re a Freak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-10-2018, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T02:48:08-07:00","id":1194472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1193884#post1193884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, don\u2019t forget Mages were human. Literally the most magical people on the planet are created by humans and you say that you can\u2019t prove Humanity is Magical.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to emphasize this heavily. I would say pretty much every progression of Magic and Mage society comes from the fact that either humanity changes the supernal directly by believe and ideals or indirectly through progressive humans becoming Mages. The idea of democracy and its benefits to a society was adopted by humas far earlier than it was by the FC. The FC were just the first Mages to adopt it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T05:14:44-07:00","id":1194492,"title":"","content":"But there's one thing speaking for democracy as a mystery though, the Free Councils can literally use it as a order tool Yantra in their spells, it has supernal meaning, so it should be far more mysterious in a occult way that what first meats the eye. <br /> And even if it's a well understood way to structure human society, it was not always so and democracy comes in many different forms. Democracy to be fair, it's a bit like porn, you know it when you see it, but sometimes you're not quite sure if it is or not. <br /> <br /> The societies of human culture that has started applying democracy has surely undermined part of exarch tyranny, but strengthen other parts. Human culture has given form to or strengthen a supernal symbol of democracy, which in turns influence the democratic process in the fallen world.<br /> And the oracles, that they're kings is an atlantean way of seeing it, kings need subjects but mages owes no allegiance toward the oracles so in the FC mind, how can they be kings, they're don't seem to judge who's worthy, they don't discriminate and they don't seem to want worship, loyalty or allegiance, neither are they interested in subjects or control. In the minds of the FC they are more egalitarian and therefore democratic, perhaps the ancient rulers of the supernal, but surely not in a kingly way. They can't represent tyranny so therefore what is lack of tyranny if not true democracy in their minds. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T05:40:47-07:00","id":1194499,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"523\" data-vbnamecard=\"523\">Poseur</a> the reason democracy can function as an Order tool is solely due to the fact that the FC taps into the Mystery of Humanity is Magical.<br /> <br /> Sure, there\u2019s a bit of magic in democracy, but it\u2019s just a subset of a bigger Mystery, by itself it isn\u2019t a grand unifying phenomenon to propel the FC into existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T05:44:41-07:00","id":1194500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1194499#post1194499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"523\" data-vbnamecard=\"523\">Poseur</a> the reason democracy can function as an Order tool is solely due to the fact that the FC taps into the Mystery of Humanity is Magical.<br /> <br /> Sure, there\u2019s a bit of magic in democracy, but it\u2019s just a subset of a bigger Mystery, by itself it isn\u2019t a grand unifying phenomenon to propel the FC into existence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In this a agree fully. I was just spiting out some random thoughts on the subject. Giving some explanation around democracy as in it self a mystery and such and how it may help with structuring the unification around the idea that humanity in itself is magical. <br /> I'm on the same line that democracy is part of the grander mystery, a sub-mystery so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:07:11-07:00","id":1194536,"title":"","content":"The thing that gets mostly missed in the translation between Nameless Order and Free Council tends to be that they aren't just a bunch of apostles doing whatever. They're ancient and recent, new magical traditions, with things like cults and even Legacies. <br /> <br /> Even cults which had sleeper and sleepwalker members with access to supernatural merits, that produced no dissonance. Hence the philosophy they developed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:16:29-07:00","id":1194537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1194536#post1194536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that gets mostly missed in the translation between Nameless Order and Free Council tends to be that they aren't just a bunch of apostles doing whatever. They're ancient and recent, new magical traditions, with things like cults and even Legacies.<br /> <br /> Even cults which had sleeper and sleepwalker members with access to supernatural merits, that produced no dissonance. Hence the philosophy they developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not get what you mean here - yes, 19th century Nameless / future Free Council is full of very old magical traditions ( like Cults or Legacies ) that did not joined Diamond before. For example, we have Dreamspeakers there. Or high number of Tremere ( based on <b>Free Council</b>, <b>Left Hand Path</b> or 2E corebook ). I was just thinking it was part of <i>Humanity is Magical</i> - that <b><i>there is</i></b> magic outside of Diamond and Seers dogma. It does not speak to me as pointing to <i>Democracy Seeks the Truth</i>, directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:39:06-07:00","id":1194543,"title":"","content":"Well, again it\u2019s because the view of the FC and the Diamond and Orders are somewhat diametrically opposed. The FC believe that magic filters from humanity up and then back down again to the Fallen. The Seers believe magic comes down from and is ruled by the Exarchs. The Diamond believe mostly the same thing, but they reject the premise that the Seers are in charge and instead believe magic comes down from the Supernal itself and that the Exarchs are interlopers.<br /> <br /> This difference in belief that the FC has means they must philosophically oppose the hierarchy of the Seers with the Exarchs at top because clearly (to them) the Exarchs are not the authors of magic. They must also reject the hierarchy of the Diamond because clearly (to them) the Supernal isn\u2019t the only source of magic and is in fact influenced by humanity. When you get to the point where you\u2019re rejecting the two prevailing hierarchical magical theories of magic you start looking around for something that fits your worldview better. Democracy in its purest form is not an hierarchical structure so it\u2019s fits what the FC see as the actual structure of reality.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a pretty clear cut line, Humanity is Magical so magic cannot be structured in an hierarchy because an hierarchy undercuts the idea that all of humanity contributes to magic. Put another way, if there are some forces, people, etc which generate magic that preempt everything else by forming an hierarchy of order then humanity cannot be magical, or at least not recognized as being as magical as it should be.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also a level of convenience to it. One Nameless group can look at another and they both say to each other, \u201cLook, we might believe different things, but I won\u2019t trample your beliefs like the Diamond or the Seers, and if you don\u2019t trample mine, and we act like we are equals we might just stand a chance of not getting squashed or absorbed by either of them.\u201d Which, canonically is exactly what happened. Democracy is keeping the different factions of the FC from stepping on each other\u2019s toes and creating a framework they can work inside of to stand together against the other two factions that at the time of the Nameless War wanted to destroy or absorb them for their \u201cheretical\u201d belief that Humanity is Magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:51:51-07:00","id":1194642,"title":"","content":"Being today in small Internet conflict with Polish LGBT Catholics organisation over LGBT issues - I finally think I get how Nameless feel inside their own Movement. Every faction was having it's own philosophy, only meshing in Nameless War because they were all were shunned by majority of Awakened society - i.e. Diamond and Seers. And, hell, they discussion and philosophical differences could be <b><i>heated </i></b>inside Nameless!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T15:50:14-07:00","id":1194655,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a big thing I try to remember when thinking of Free Council villains is that not all of them are completely accepting of the whole &quot;all beliefs are equal&quot;, &quot;live and let live&quot; democracy thing, and just joined because they didn't want to join the other Orders and have to follow the Orders' cults. You could have a rabbi Mage that is secretly planning to get rid of or otherwise usurp all the &quot;pagan&quot; Mages in his Consilium.<br /> <br /> EDIT: bad example, more likely to be a political Banisher","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T14:42:54-07:00","id":1194988,"title":"","content":"&quot;Humanity is Magical&quot; isn't the only Mystery, Mrmdubois. <br /> <br /> &quot;Hierarchy fosters the Lie&quot; Really? Is that even true? Why would it be so? There are many ways to investigate the mysteries related to that, from seeking hierarchies that <i>don't</i> help hide lies, to investigating instances where it did to see at what point and in which ways it does. <br /> <br /> &quot;Destroy all followers of the Lie&quot; isn't as obviously a mystery. You need to know how to identify your enemies and figure out how to stop them, all of which certainly involves Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The nature of the Lie, itself, is a major part of all three tenets. How can humanity punch through to enlightenment without help? How can we remove hiding places so that operates most efficiently? How can we stop those who are preventing this goal?<br /> <br /> The Lie, itself, is the primary central Mystery of the Free Council, for good or ill.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T15:38:26-07:00","id":1195006,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> I didn\u2019t say it was the only Mystery. I said it\u2019s the major focus of the FC as a Mystery as opposed to democracy which isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> You're dead wrong about the Lie being their central Mystery though. Sure, they investigate it, its agents, and how to dismantle it, all worthwhile mysteries in their own right. They reason they give a shit about the Lie though is because it gets in the way of and impedes their investigation into the actual Mystery of Humanity is Magical.<br /> <br /> Because for some reason I feel like elaborating to someone so clearly in the wrong, if the Lie was the central Mystery of the FC it would be more central to their doctrine rather than something that must be combated to experience and engage in with than their actual central Mystery. Humanity is Magical.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, if the Lie was the Mystery they held dearest then that would be one of their core tenets instead of Humanity is Magical. I feel I've sufficiently pointed out that the other two tenets are a way to protect that one central Mystery. What you're saying is pure speculation. The FC engages the Lie, sure, but it's not what they're about. If it was then it would be in print, your inability to grok that just points out your inability to understand what's presented in the text. Which, from what I've seen in conversations between you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> is far from unprecedented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-13-2018, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T21:36:23-07:00","id":1195957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1195006#post1195006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The FC engages the Lie, sure, but it's not what they're about. If it was then it would be in print...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. Even the section on Humanity is Magical makes a big point of the martial interpretation. &quot;Destroy Followers of the Lie&quot; is clear. &quot;Democracy Seeks the Truth&quot; is far less directly focused on the Lie than was &quot;Hierarchy Fosters the Lie&quot;, but it still applies as a weapon against the Lie.<br /> <br /> Humanity being magical is certainly an important Mystery to the order. So is the Lie. It's not a duality, precisely, but it is quite similar. Much as a doctor studies both healthy and diseased states, those who fight the lie study Humanity and the Lie in different ways. Identifying targets or harvesting/inventing flat hierarchies may often intersect with Humanity's nature and those Mysteries, but they <i>always</i> involve the Lie in some way. <br /> <br /> The Free Council fights the Lie. They use humanity's magical nature as both a tool in the fight and impetus, but the underlying focus of their organizational attention <i>is</i> on the fight.<br /> <br /> If you don't like that or, heck, just don't see it, it's not a big deal. I would appreciate a less hostile tone in the future. That was unwarranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T04:24:55-07:00","id":1196443,"title":"","content":"With the showing of <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Gr8iupVYfKmNj0xuSir7lEvkdw8AsLbs/view\" target=\"_blank\">new <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> preview about Aedes and Supernal Boons</a> - I wonder if not make this 'Democracy spreads around the world' as Mystery connected with Aedes of Mind ( or something similar ) popping all around XIX century, influencing the minds of Sleepers? Retelling what Hermit was saying at start of the topic....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1192129#post1192129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And said way happens to be an anachronistic set of governance nobody really cared about for the past few centuries. Which suddenly rose as the dominant political ideology of the world, almost as if the World itself was backing up the Council\u2019s claims. That is a Mystery enough for me... but then again, I major in politics, so I\u2019m biased towards things like this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If this would be Aedes of Mind ( or Space - cause 'closeness' democracy brings ? ) it would make it Pandemonium Aedes, yes?<br /> <br /> Text even points that places where Ochemata are showing can become Aedes, so we have direct relations with <b>Mage</b> canon... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:50:52-07:00","id":1196483,"title":"","content":"It would be better to have the Aedes forming from the rise of democracy rather than the other way around, that would reinforce the central Mystery of the Free Council that Humanity is Magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:54:15-07:00","id":1196485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1195957#post1195957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. Even the section on Humanity is Magical makes a big point of the martial interpretation. &quot;Destroy Followers of the Lie&quot; is clear. &quot;Democracy Seeks the Truth&quot; is far less directly focused on the Lie than was &quot;Hierarchy Fosters the Lie&quot;, but it still applies as a weapon against the Lie.<br /> <br /> Humanity being magical is certainly an important Mystery to the order. So is the Lie. It's not a duality, precisely, but it is quite similar. Much as a doctor studies both healthy and diseased states, those who fight the lie study Humanity and the Lie in different ways. Identifying targets or harvesting/inventing flat hierarchies may often intersect with Humanity's nature and those Mysteries, but they <i>always</i> involve the Lie in some way.<br /> <br /> The Free Council fights the Lie. They use humanity's magical nature as both a tool in the fight and impetus, but the underlying focus of their organizational attention <i>is</i> on the fight.<br /> <br /> If you don't like that or, heck, just don't see it, it's not a big deal. I would appreciate a less hostile tone in the future. That was unwarranted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about my tone earlier. I still disagree that the Lie is central to the FC, or rather that if it is it's only because it's in the way. It's true after all that they have to deal with the Lie, but only because it interferes with what they're actually interested in. Looking over your last post though I think we're actually mostly on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:22:55-07:00","id":1196650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1196443#post1196443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this would be Aedes of Mind ( or Space - cause 'closeness' democracy brings ? ) it would make it Pandemonium Aedes, yes?<br /> <br /> Text even points that places where Ochemata are showing can become Aedes, so we have direct relations with <b>Mage</b> canon... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't say I agree with the Free Council's core ethos being Democracy nor Democracy being a Supernally deduced concept, mostly for the same reasons Mrmdubois said. BUT, if I were to accept such premises anyway, and connect the Supernal to democracy...<br /> <br /> The Aether dictates to us that Power can only be wielded by those with the strength to Command it. The masses are rising up, and perhaps for the first time in history, are seizing control and claiming sovereignty for themselves.<br /> <br /> Arcadia promises to us that those who make their own Choices are entitled to its Consequences, for the better or the worse. The people are now choosing their own leaders; what will become of such choices?<br /> <br /> Pandemonium whispers to us that only by Confronting barriers can we overcome them, and by Transgressing them we become ourselves. The millennia-old social structure is being called to question by those who were once deemed inferior.<br /> <br /> The Primal Wild sings to us that when the worlds conflict, one must stand on not either worlds but their Boundaries to seek Intercession and harmony. When each man is now a shaman hosting his ideology as god and facing down others as outsiders, a conflict of worlds looms inevitable.<br /> <br /> Stygia teaches us that even though all things will end and meet Transition, within its vicissitudes Permanence can be found for the diligent and determined. Nothing will be like before in the fires of revolution, and when the flames subside what will remain?<br /> <br /> So it's not just Pandemonium - all Supernal Worlds/Realms and Paths have something to say. Now, how to arrange these into solid mechanics for Aedes effects is another story... but I'm sure you or anybody else can think of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T21:38:46-07:00","id":1196710,"title":"","content":"Well, we will see - I wonder if there will be some 'dropping it's Supernal imprint' Aedes. Of those of Prima Wild shown in preview, look like Singing Path is more adequate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T06:10:17-07:00","id":1196772,"title":"","content":"For some dumb reason I\u2019ve been thinking about this, and I came to the conclusion the Aedes should also be geographically distinct occurring in areas where democracy is happening so you can work in the Humanity is Magical angle. <br /> <br /> They should also be layered drawing from 21C Hermit\u2019s quote up there. There\u2019s literally nothing stopping one Aedes from one Path being in the same place as an Aedes from another Path because to both those Paths only one Aede exists. There\u2019s also nothing stopping Aedes from different Paths having a sort of similar core theme.<br /> <br /> Then you get your Mages from different Paths together and talk about their different, but similar Aedes and boom you get FC. It\u2019s perfect, you get to completely sidestep the messiness of people dealing with people because the Supernal told them to do democracy folks! And somehow it\u2019s also magically not still Seers lite! /sarcasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T22:43:21-07:00","id":1197047,"title":"","content":"As I think about including Gifted - 'magical scientists' template from <b>Mage Chronicle's Guide</b> - as players option to choose from - I wonder how to deal with Aedes Mystery. Gifted, at least in 1E <b>MGC</b>, did not have Mage Sight. If Aedes are in Supernal World of each Realm - they will not be able to percieve them. So should I open to Gfted 'glimpses' general Supernal? Or just let other Paths share their Mage Sight? Thiniking about it - Gifted 2E update will need it's own topic. But you thoughts are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:13:25-07:00","id":1197102,"title":"","content":"So...you\u2019re done playing Mage and are going to make a crossover game about the creation of the FC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:16:07-07:00","id":1197104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1197102#post1197102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...you\u2019re done playing Mage and are going to make a crossover game about the creation of the FC?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifted are mentioned as the Hack to the Mage - in the official book of <b>M</b><b>age Chronicle's Guide. </b>So it's still in the bounds of Mage as gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:18:49-07:00","id":1197107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191993-creation-of-free-council-equality-as-mystery?p=1197104#post1197104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifted are mentioned as the Hack to the Mage - in the official book of <b>M</b><b>age Chronicle's Guide. </b>So it's still in the bounds of Mage as gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, it\u2019s a hack using Mage rules that isn\u2019t actually Mage. It\u2019s like all the folks that keep hacking Ascension to have Awakening mechanics.<br /> <br /> Except you want to keep regular Mages in. So it\u2019s a crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:48:31-07:00","id":1197118,"title":"","content":"In response to your answer in the wrong thread because you have too many of them:<br /> <br /> It's simple math. X+Y=Z. X+Y=X isn't possible except in the case of Y being 0. The Gifted are not a value of 0 as they do add changes to the game to make it a game that is different than Mage. If Mage stands for X and Gifted stands for Y then you get Z of crossover. Doesn't matter if they're running on the same dice engine, all of the CoD lines do that. It's still crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}